        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "de13b34d-24da-5a6e-b0ee-d0174bae9691",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jayaprakash Narayan, Prakash Ambedkar, B. R. Ambedkar\n- Organizations: People's Union for Civil Liberties, People's Union for Civil Liberties and Democratic Rights, Bharatiya Republican Party - Bahujan Mahasangh\n- Awards: Bharat Ratna\n- Places: India\n\nFacts:\n- In 1976, Jayaprakash Narayan formed the People's Union for Civil Liberties in India as the People's Union for Civil Liberties and Democratic Rights.\n- The People's Union for Civil Liberties is a human rights body in India.\n- In 1999, Jayaprakash Narayan was posthumously awarded the Bharat Ratna in recognition of his social work.\n- The Bharat Ratna is the highest civilian award of the Republic of India.\n- Prakash Ambedkar founded the Bharatiya Republican Party - Bahujan Mahasangh, an Indian political party.\n- Prakash Ambedkar is the grandson of B. R. Ambedkar.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
