        "text": "Page: Jayaprakash Narayan. Sentence: In 1999, he was posthumously awarded the Bharat Ratna, India's highest civilian award, in recognition of his social work.\nPage: Bharat Ratna. Sentence: The Bharat Ratna (] ; \"Jewel of India\") is the highest civilian award of the Republic of India.\nPage: People's Union for Civil Liberties. Sentence: People's Union for Civil Liberties (PUCL) is a human rights body formed in India in 1976 by socialist leader Jayaprakash Narayan, as the People's Union for Civil Liberties and Democratic Rights (PUCLDR).\nPage: Bharatiya Republican Party. Sentence: The Bharatiya Republican Party - Bahujan Mahasangh (भरिप, भारतिय रिपब्लीकन पक्ष-बहुजन महासंघ) (BRP) is the Indian political party founded by advocate Prakash Ambedkar (Grand Son of Bharatratna Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar).",
